# ThunderVox — site-local values and switches (template)
# ======================================================
# Copy to local.cfg and fill in for your server. local.cfg is gitignored and is
# pulled into kamailio.cfg by "include_file" — never commit the filled-in copy.
#
# substdef performs a textual replace everywhere in the config, including inside
# strings, so a value can appear both bare (listen/advertise) and inside JSON
# (push body) with the same definition.

# ---- Server address: at least one of the two below must be set. ----

# SIP domain (preferred): the DNS name that resolves to this server. Devices
# register to it and dial through it (sip:102@sip.example.com). When set, the
# core works through it - advertised in Via/Record-Route and treated as "myself".
#!substdef "!TVX_SIP_DOMAIN!sip.example.com!g"

# Server public IP. Advertised instead of the domain when TVX_SIP_DOMAIN is not
# set; otherwise only accepted as "myself" for devices that dial by raw IP.
# Keep it equal to TVX_PUBLIC_IP in the deployment .env (thundervox/deploy/.env, which feeds rtpengine).
#!substdef "!TVX_PUBLIC_IP!203.0.113.10!g"

# Token the provisioning server expects from the core on its internal API
# (X-CORE-TOKEN): the same value as TVX_CORE_TOKEN in the deployment .env. With
# it set, the core reports call events to the server (call log, dashboard) and
# may ask it to wake phones (TVX_PUSH_WAIT). Leave it out only when there is no
# server. The push gateway itself (URL, auth header) is set on the console's
# Integration page, not here.
#!substdef "!TVX_CORE_TOKEN!replace-with-the-core-token-of-dot-env!g"

# Where the provisioning server listens. The default is the compose layout
# (host network, loopback); uncomment only when the server runs elsewhere.
##!substdef "!TVX_SERVER_URL!http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/v1!g"

# Provisioning database: the tvx_sip role the server's migration V3 creates, its
# password = TVX_SIP_DB_PASSWORD of the deployment .env. Only used with
# TVX_PROVISIONING. No '!' in the password - it delimits this substdef.
#!substdef "!TVX_DB_URL!postgres://tvx_sip:replace-with-tvx-sip-password@127.0.0.1:5432/thundervox!g"


# ---- Switches: uncomment to enable. Everything below is OFF when absent. ----

# Accounts and registrations from the provisioning server: digest auth of
# REGISTER and INVITE against its database (passwords issued in the console),
# registrations stored there too. Requires TVX_SIP_DOMAIN (the digest realm -
# must equal TVX_SIP_HOST of the .env the server hashes with) and TVX_DB_URL.
# Switch it on only after every device got its password in the console: from
# that moment a device without one can neither register nor call.
##!define TVX_PROVISIONING

# App clients (numbers 1...) are push-first: their INVITEs are parked for the
# wake window and the provisioning server is asked to wake the phones (http on
# loopback; the server delivers the push to the operator's backend configured
# on the Integration page); the devices that register after the push are rung,
# all of them in parallel. Requires TVX_CORE_TOKEN. Without it an offline callee
# gets "480 Temporarily Unavailable" immediately and a registered one is simply
# rung - the right mode while no push gateway is set.
##!define TVX_PUSH_WAIT

# Request-rate guard per source IP (pike): >32 requests / 2 s -> dropped.
##!define TVX_ANTIFLOOD

# Accept SIPS on 5061 in addition to plain 5060. Requires TVX_SIP_DOMAIN (a
# certificate is issued for a name, not for an IP) and a filled-in tls.cfg next
# to this file - its template ships in the image as
# /etc/kamailio/tls.cfg.example. Plain 5060 keeps working for devices whose
# firmware has no TLS.
##!define TVX_TLS
